/*  FUNCTION NAME:      NEIGHBOURS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the A1-style addresses of all cells within a given distance of a centre cell (Manhattan, Chebyshev, or Euclidean), excluding the centre.*/
/*  RETURNS:            column of address (text), the cells within distance of the centre, excluding it, nearest ring first and each ring clockwise from north (the library's direction order, as _dirAll)
    PARAMETERS:
        centerCell      (Required) Centre cell address as text (e.g. "C3"), or a cell containing one. Scalar only.
        distance        (Optional) Maximum distance from the centre; cells with 0 < dist <= distance are returned. Default 1. Non-integer values are meaningful for the Euclidean metric (e.g. 1.5 includes diagonals).
        metric          (Optional) Distance metric: 0 Manhattan (default, 4-directional), 1 Chebyshev (8-directional, diagonals count as 1), 2 Euclidean (straight-line). Mirrors CELLDIST.
        grid            (Optional) A grid range or array bounding the result - neighbours outside it are dropped. Omitted, results are bounded only by row 1 and column A (no upper limit, so neighbours past XFD or row 1048576 are returned, e.g. XFE5).
        origin          (Optional) Top-left anchor as a workbook reference - a single cell or a range (a range's top-left is used). Anchors an in-memory grid to a worksheet position - matches GRIDAREA/SUBGRID convention. Ignored when grid is omitted. Defaults to the grid's own top-left - inferred for a reference, (1,1) for an array.
    EXAMPLE:            =NEIGHBOURS("C3") -> C2, D3, C4, B3 (the 4 Manhattan neighbours N, E, S, W)
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-08-08  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-06  Claude      Decode at the _mult constant (was a local 16385, which misread 100000-packed positions passed through TOPOS); with grid omitted, no longer cut at XFD / row 1048576 (#380)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
                        2026-11-16  Claude      Order is now ring by ring (nearest first), each ring clockwise from north, as _dirAll; was reading order (#478)
*/
NEIGHBOURS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [centerCell],
    [distance],
    [metric],
    [grid],
    [origin],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        safeMult, _mult,
        rad, IF(ISOMITTED(distance), 1, @distance),
        met, IF(ISOMITTED(metric), 0, @metric),
        pos, TOPOS(@centerCell, safeMult),
        ctrRow, INT(pos / safeMult),
        ctrCol, MOD(pos, safeMult),
        span, INT(rad),
        dRow, SEQUENCE(2 * span + 1, 1, -span),
        dCol, SEQUENCE(1, 2 * span + 1, -span),
        distGrid, IF(met = 2, SQRT(dRow ^ 2 + dCol ^ 2),
                  IF(met = 1, IF(ABS(dRow) > ABS(dCol), ABS(dRow), ABS(dCol)),
                              ABS(dRow) + ABS(dCol))),
        cellRow, ctrRow + dRow,
        cellCol, ctrCol + dCol,
        baseRow, IF(ISOMITTED(grid), 1, IF(ISOMITTED(origin), IFERROR(MIN(ROW(grid)), 1), MIN(ROW(origin)))),
        baseCol, IF(ISOMITTED(grid), 1, IF(ISOMITTED(origin), IFERROR(MIN(COLUMN(grid)), 1), MIN(COLUMN(origin)))),
        maxRow, IF(ISOMITTED(grid), ctrRow + span, baseRow + ROWS(grid) - 1),
        maxCol, IF(ISOMITTED(grid), ctrCol + span, baseCol + COLUMNS(grid) - 1),
        inBounds, (cellRow >= baseRow) * (cellRow <= maxRow) * (cellCol >= baseCol) * (cellCol <= maxCol),
        keep, (distGrid > 0) * (distGrid <= rad) * inBounds,
        addrGrid, IF(OR(MAX(cellCol) > 16384, MAX(cellRow) > 1048576), CELLAT(cellRow, cellCol), ADDRESS(cellRow, cellCol, 4)),
        bearing, IFERROR(MOD(ATAN2(-dRow, dCol), 2 * PI()), 0),
        addrs, TOCOL(IF(keep = 1, addrGrid, NA()), 2),
        rings, TOCOL(IF(keep = 1, distGrid, NA()), 2),
        bearings, TOCOL(IF(keep = 1, bearing, NA()), 2),
        result, IF(ISTEXT(pos), pos, IFERROR(SORTBY(addrs, rings, 1, bearings, 1), NA())),
        result
)
);
